## C1. Block Fitting bound: a single DVR row module and exact matrix units

Read actual Lib/General/Algebra/BlockFittingBound.lean
9107737c82be74338b8843ab315bf11d1b186d51, exists_rows_addVal_det_le;
New/Selmer/RibetFirstOrder.lean a05cb18d1ee62520f104d41361099db4b23cbe1f,
actual B0 construction and final coefficient H.

Let O be the actual DVR, A an O-algebra, psi:A -> Mat_d(O) onto,
N an A-submodule of A^I, p nonzero, and b<v(p). The common
annihilator of N on ((O/p)^d)^I is contained in Z with length <=b.
For t in N write M(t)=[psi(t_i)]_{i in I}, a d-by-D matrix, D=d|I|.
Let R in O^D be the O-span of all coordinate rows of all M(t).
The common annihilator modulo p is exactly the annihilator of R.
Indeed the matrix equations are equivalent to each scalar coordinate
row equation. There is no extra factor d in this identification.

Let R'=R+p O^D. Since p is nonzero, R' is a full-rank DVR lattice.
Smith normal form gives invariant exponents e_i between 0 and v(p),
and a basis matrix H with v(det H)=sum e_i. The common annihilator
modulo p has length exactly sum e_i: after invertible coordinate
changes, coordinate i is killed by a uniformizer to the e_i, and
the annihilator in O/p has length e_i. Thus v(det H)<=b.
This uses the ordinary DVR Smith theorem, with the actual full-rank
and finitely generated hypotheses (O is Noetherian, D finite).
For D=0 the empty determinant is 1, and the conclusion is immediate.

Write the rows H_j=r_j+p u_j with r_j in R, u_j integral.
Every r in R can be realized as the first row of some M(t), all
other rows zero: take the linear combination of matrix units E_1c
times M(t) for the coordinate rows forming r. Lift each scalar
multiple of E_1c through surjective psi, and use A-submodule
closure of N. More generally, place each r in any prescribed row
using E_ac. Group the D rows r_j in |I| blocks of d; in each block
sum the corresponding lifted row realizations. This constructs
one B in Mat_I(A) with EVERY block row in N and whose block-expanded
psi(B) has rows r_j exactly. No need for a simultaneous arbitrary
entry lift that might leave N.

Then det psi(B) == det H mod p by multilinearity (equivalently
determinants commute with reduction). Because v(det H)<=b<v(p),
the two valuations are equal by the strict ultrametric property.
Hence

    v(det block(psi(B))) = v(det H) = length(ann(N mod p)) <= b.

This is the actual exists_rows_addVal_det_le conclusion. It uses
surjectivity and the strict b<v(p) essentially; no proof of an
unconditional annihilator bound or removal of the actual cocycle
hypothesis. At the B0 caller retain span rho(pi)=Mat_r(O), the
specialization X=0, and the native injection of annihilator
coordinates into obeyingCocycles with tau and gamma zero. The
injection is not proved by Smith normal form.

## C2. Exact coefficient extraction in the actual ribet_first_order proof

Let Lambda=O[X_j], finite J, P=prod_j X_j, m its squarefree exponent.
I_q is the support ideal generated by monomials whose exponent is
NOT <=m coordinatewise. This is an ideal since its support is upward
closed. In particular every polynomial in I_q has zero coefficient
at every divisor of P. Partition J by the actual ordered map ty,
P_e=prod_{ty(j)=e} X_j, Q_e=prod_{ty(j)<e} X_j.
The native exists_mem_fittingIdeal_block and sup_smul_top_le
produce d_e=Gamma_e P_e+zeta_e with Q_e zeta_e in I_q.
The latter is exactly the colon-ideal membership in hI; no claim
that zeta_e alone belongs to I_q.

Use the first-error telescoping identity, ordered by e:
    prod_e d_e - prod_e (Gamma_e P_e)
      = sum_e [prod_{i<e}(Gamma_i P_i)] zeta_e [prod_{i>e} d_i].
Every summand has Q_e zeta_e as a factor, so belongs to I_q.
The identity follows by successively replacing factors in order
and subtracting; no positivity, norm, cancellation estimate or
bound on the number of terms. Hence for ANY polynomial D,
    D prod_e d_e == D (prod_e Gamma_e) P    mod I_q.
For any exponent n<=m, the right side has coefficient zero unless
n=m; at m its coefficient is exactly constantCoeff(D prod_e Gamma_e).
This proves the actual coefficient filter hd' used in H; in
particular it is valid when some P_e=1, and for the empty J.
It does not replace the triangle lemma that produces Gamma_e.

At the actual H, the retained Cramer trace ideal construction,
normalizer k, selectors q_e, and matrix block equalities give
D_y=det(block(psi_y(B0))) C a^t, where
    a=(prod_v o_v(1)) C^|s|.
Thus at the distinguished pi the extracted coefficient (before
the algebraMap O L) is
    c = det(block(psi_pi(B0))(0)) C a^t prod_e Gamma_e(0).
The exact valuation budget, before bounding, is
    v(c) = v(det B0(0)) + v(C)
           + t sum_v v(o_v(1)) + t|s| v(C)
           + sum_e v(Gamma_e(0)).
Combine C1 and the actual block triangle bound
v(Gamma_e(0))<=b_e+(|I_e|+|s|)v(C). Since the I_e partition J,
    v(c) <= b0 + sum_e b_e + t sum_v v(o_v(1))
                  + (2t|s|+|J|+1)v(C).
This is exactly the conclusion budget of ribet_first_order.
If some factors are zero interpret valuations in the extended
nonnegative value monoid; a finite upper budget forces nonzero.
No estimate or loss from the squarefree extraction. The exact
RibetElement.lean caller instantiates u' from the simultaneous
twisted block lattices, uses the native trace ideal, tame/crystalline
Selmer restrictions and hasTriangleCost_tateTwist. Those premises
remain open where not yet human-derived; the final rowBudget
comparison is not closed by this coefficient calculation.

